# AI-SDLC Orchestrator plugin — brownfield-mode state
#
# The plugin keeps per-project state under `.sdlc/`. Most of it is
# team-shared and belongs in git; a few files are personal or
# ephemeral and must NOT be committed.
#
# Add this fragment (or its lines) to your project's .gitignore.
# The plugin only offers this at first-run Gate 0; it never
# appends to your .gitignore without asking.

# Personal / per-developer state — never commit
.sdlc/local/

# Optional: uncomment to also ignore support bundles (they redact secrets
# but include debug logs and provenance excerpts, which some teams prefer
# to keep out of the repo history)
# .sdlc/support-bundle-*.tar.gz

# What stays committed (do NOT ignore):
#   .sdlc/project.json         — team fingerprint (stack, test cmd, off-limits)
#   .sdlc/policy.yaml          — team routing policy override (if used)
#   .sdlc/ledger.md            — human-readable run history
#   .sdlc/ledger.json          — machine mirror of the ledger
#   .sdlc/runs/**              — per-run frozen records (packets, provenance, reports)
#   .sdlc/baseline/**          — living project baseline (discovery + stack profile)
